      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Ultracold atoms in optical lattices turned quantum many-body models into controllable laboratory systems, enabling clean tests of phenomena that are difficult to isolate in solids.",
        "attribution": "Bloch and Greiner represent pivotal experimental work, while Zoller helped develop the theoretical vision for quantum simulation; the field's progress is notably collective.",
        "maturity": "The platform has been established for decades and supports increasingly precise studies, though its reach as a general simulator continues to develop.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The boundary between foundational demonstrations and subsequent advances is broad, with several groups making essential contributions."
        ]
      }
    },
