        "Edward Witten"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Gauge/gravity duality has had extraordinary influence, connecting quantum field theory and gravity and supplying powerful tools for problems in both fields.",
        "attribution": "Maldacena's conjecture and Witten's development and clarification are central contributions. The proposal reflects the core origin and early establishment of the correspondence.",
        "maturity": "The mathematical framework and its applications are highly developed, but the physical relevance of the correspondence to our universe remains unresolved.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The duality lacks direct experimental confirmation and is formulated in settings unlike observed cosmology.",
          "Whether a primarily theoretical result of this kind meets the discovery standard for the prize is uncertain."
        ]
      }
    },
